          "id": 3821698,
          "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjM4MjE2OTg=",
          "gravatar_id": "",
          "url": "https://api.github.com/users/donaldchen",
          "type": "User",
          "site_admin": false
        },
        "labels": [],
        "state": "closed",
        "locked": false,
        "assignee": null,
        "assignees": [],
        "milestone": null,
        "comments": 1,
        "created_at": "2022-12-09T23:13:52Z",
        "updated_at": "2023-01-11T22:02:17Z",
        "closed_at": "2023-01-11T22:02:17Z",
        "author_association": "NONE",
        "active_lock_reason": null,
        "draft": false,
        "pull_request": {
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/discord/react-native-orientation/pulls/6",
          "merged_at": "2023-01-11T22:02:17Z"
        },
        "body": "Emit the orientation degrees changes from Kotlin to JS, so the JS can determine the device orientation (different from the app orientation). That way, the react native app can request changing an orientation without locking it by\r\n- first locking to an orientation\r\n- waiting for the device orientation to match the orientation lock\r\n- then unlocking the orientation\r\n\r\nlike in https://stackoverflow.com/questions/22848222/toggling-fullscreen-orientation-like-youtube/23489227#23489227",
